      "classes": "1: NO MATCH -- A credit agreement is not a payment, interest, or amortization schedule.\n2: NO MATCH -- A credit facility is not any listed schedule, transaction, or rate convention.\n3: NO MATCH -- Amortization is the reduction of debt, not the schedule showing it.\n4: NO MATCH -- No candidate represents an increase in debt through unpaid interest.\n5: NO MATCH -- Calculating interest is distinct from resetting its rate.\n6: NO MATCH -- No candidate represents available borrowing capacity.\n7: NO MATCH -- No candidate represents a loan secured by collateral.\n8: NO MATCH -- No candidate represents a collateralized loan."
